From 3fe8b72e00141aef2cc540b12536d9f7c340276e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 04:25:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10360/11362] Add efficiency and generalization to the
 dashboard; decline a submission score

The operator asked for an estimated efficiency score and an estimated submission
score. One is now on the dashboard, one is deliberately not, and the second
decision is the substantive one.

EFFICIENCY: THE FIRST VERSION WAS A FABRICATED CAPABILITY CLAIM, caught before
shipping. It applied the competition's own rule --
`min(human_baseline/agent, 1.0) ** 2`, from docs.arcprize.org/methodology -- over
the banked solve artifacts and returned a uniform 1.000. Real arithmetic over the
wrong quantity: the stored `solution` is the WINNING PATH REPLAYED, so it is
1.2x-5.3x shorter than a human who had to explore (ar25 157/66, g50t 253/48,
ft09 78/25). Every game pinned to the cap, which is the IMPLAUSIBLE_PERFECT
shape.

The cap is what hid it. Uncapped, the same data says "the saved path is ~2.8x
shorter than human exploration" -- true, and obviously not a capability claim. So
the line now leads with DISCOVERY COST NOT MEASURED and reports the raw ratio
with its coverage (22 games, 3 unmeasured) and its provenance
(development_proxy). A mutation that re-applies the cap fails the suite.

SUBMISSION SCORE: DECLINED, and the dashboard says "not measured" instead. The
competition scores HIDDEN games. All 25 public games are cleared by hand-built
per-game GameAdapters that by construction do not transfer -- that gap is the
entire reason the generalization program exists. A public-set number in the
headline position would be read as a leaderboard prediction it cannot support,
and every relevant flag is still `unevaluated`.

In its place: `generaliz.`, counting levels whose solve carries
`solve_provenance: live_agent_self_discovery` -- the only configuration
resembling first contact on a hidden game. It currently reads "not measured",
which is correct: every solve artifact is development_proxy. Returning 0 was
rejected because a zero reads as a measured result; a mutation that turns
"not measured" into a zero fails the suite.

14 tests; 5/5 mutations RED (ratio re-capped, caveat dropped from the line,
generalization counting every solve, a missing side scoring 0 instead of None,
"not measured" becoming a zero). Restores byte-identical.

